#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
CodeMind Batch Runner — click to run, set up in the browser.

Double-click this file (or the launcher it creates next to itself). It opens a
dashboard in your web browser, asks for the server address, the playbook(s) and
the repositories the first time only, and then runs the batch. Everything after
that is buttons.

No installation. Python 3.9+ and nothing else — the whole app is this one file.

Design guarantees
-----------------
crash-safe      every state change is written to SQLite before the next network
                call; if the app is closed mid-batch, restarting re-attaches to
                the runs already in flight instead of resubmitting them
idempotent      a repository already finished is never run twice
bounded         2 parallel runs by default, paced submits, circuit breaker, and
                a hard 30-minute deadline per run
observable      live dashboard, per-run JSON, CSV export, offline HTML report
shardable       split one repo list across many machines with Advanced > Shard

Advanced / server use:
    python codemind_batch.py --headless        run from codemind.json, no browser
    python codemind_batch.py --port 8080       pin the dashboard port
    python codemind_batch.py --demo            self test against a built-in mock
"""

